Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:08:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/15] migrations: skip-gate for replica processes

Intent: JELLYFIN_SKIP_MIGRATIONS=true turns migration execution into a
checkpoint: zero pending means one info line and normal startup; any
pending fails fast naming the count and pointing at the migration Job
(--mode MigrateSystem). Replicas set the env, the Job does not, so the
Job's migrate path is untouched. "Pending" is read from the same sources
the runner uses: the history table, the migrations assembly the active
provider configures (an external provider such as the PostgreSQL plugin
brings its own) and the code migrations of every stage, not only the
stage being entered. Ported onto the 12.x MigrateStepAsync, which now
returns whether anything was applied: a gated process applied nothing
and returns false, so it never triggers the post-migration database
optimisation on a replica boot. The pass is cached per service instance,
not per process: Program builds a new service for each in-process
restart, so a restart after a backup restore checks the restored history
again. Includes the gate tests.
Ceiling: the gate compares history with the migrations assembly, not
the runtime model with the schema; a provider whose migrations lag the
model passes it (EF does not check pending model changes for Jellyfin's
explicit-target MigrateAsync either). bool.TryParse accepts only
true/false.
Drop when: upstream grows an equivalent gate.

